 "note": "Names a Riftgate chassis must not wear: the machines of the properties this game's designs sit nearest. Ryan, 28 September: not a copyright worry, the point is that a design reads as ours or as a knowing homage, never as a copy. The validator refuses a chassis whose name or id matches any name here exactly (case, spaces, hyphens ignored; sharing a word is fine) unless the entry's design object records why it stays under name_clash. BattleTech is listed whole, every 'Mech, because a Huntsman or a Griffin reads as a lift as surely as a Timber Wolf. battletech_animals repeats the Earth-animal subset grouped by kind, as a reading aid for choosing nicknames; every name in it is also in sources.battletech.",
